    "comprehensive_coverage": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "Coverage is badly unbalanced across the three named sub-cases. Division by ten, a hundred and a thousand accounts for about half the set, from 70 divided by 10 up to 6540 divided by 10, while the with-remainder sub-case is carried by only two samples, 51 by 8 and 60 by 7. A sub-case represented by two items out of fifteen cannot certify that remainder handling works across divisors."
    },
    "cognitive_capacity": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Dividends are read rather than long-divided in the power-of-ten cases, the exact divisions use familiar table facts extended to three digits as with 448 by 7, and the remainder notation is the standard Grade 3 form."
    },
    "variant_comprehensiveness": {
